| !SparkFS.Load -- set SparkFS up at the command line, without the desktop,
| as !Run and !RunImage do: SparkFS started afresh with its !Run's settings
| (memory from a dynamic area, the image filing system on, names up to 255
| characters, 32 archives open, an image closed after 5 seconds unused,
| changes cached), then its file extensions and the types it leaves
| uncompressed (its Config.Extensions and Config.NoCo, as its !RunImage
| gives them), then the codecs, which register their archive types as image
| filing systems: all ten, as !RunImage starts each one its Choices installs
| (the Modules directory's: Zip, Tar, Spark -- Spark, ArcFS and PK arc --
| Lzh, ARJ, Cab, CPIO, Zoo, McStuffit -- StuffIt, PackIt, Compact Pro -- and
| PackdDir).  SparkFS and the codecs are the ROM's: each is started again
| (*RMReInit), as RMLoad would load it afresh -- a codec registers its
| archive types as it starts, and only once SparkFSImage 1 has said to.
| The scrap directory: Spark$Scrap if it is set, else Wimp$ScrapDir (this
| directory is in the ROM, and cannot be written).
SetEval SparkFS$Memory -2
Set SparkFSRes$Dir <SparkFS$Dir>.Resources.UK
If ("<Spark$Scrap>" = "") AND ("<Wimp$ScrapDir>" <> "") Then Set Spark$Scrap <Wimp$ScrapDir>
RMReInit SparkFS
SparkFSImage 1
SparkFSTruncate 255
SparkFSBuffers 32
SparkFSImageTimeout 5
SparkFSCache 1
SparkFSMemory 27K 4808K
Obey <SparkFS$Dir>.Resources.Extensions
Obey <SparkFS$Dir>.Resources.NoCo
RMReInit Zip
RMReInit Tar
RMReInit Spark
RMReInit Lzh
RMReInit ARJ
RMReInit Cab
RMReInit CPIO
RMReInit Zoo
RMReInit McStuffit
RMReInit PackdDir
